R['lay_summary']=("The plan predicts the shape of tiny fluid-filled balls of kidney-type cells using a computer model. I redid the sums from the published data. Most numbers check out, but one formula was written upside down and several tests are too weak to ever say no. The biggest problem is that each cell type was photographed on different days, so a difference between cell types cannot be told apart from a difference between days. It is like comparing exam marks from two different schools in two different years. I suggest keeping three tests in a stricter form and dropping two that have no usable data.")
